course: dictionary
lesson: 15119
title: A word for hello
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A salutation is a greeting. It is a word or action that says hello, like «Good morning» or a friendly wave.
explain: In a letter or email, the salutation is the greeting at the start, such as «Dear Sam,». It comes before the main message, so look at the top of a letter to find it.
explain: Salutation can also be a jokey, old-fashioned hello. In Charlotte's Web, the spider Charlotte greets Wilbur with «Salutations!». Context helps you see that this is a friendly greeting, not a goodbye.
fact: A salutation is a greeting.
fact: «Good morning» and a wave can both be salutations.
fact: In a letter, the salutation is the greeting at the start, like «Dear Sir or Madam».
fact: «Salutations!» is an old-fashioned, playful way to say hello.
fact: A letter has parts: address, date, salutation, body and sign-off.
exercise: «The students gave their teacher a cheerful salutation as she walked in.» What is a salutation here? | A test paper | *A greeting, like hello | A loud noise made by a bell | A lunch box
exercise: In a letter, which line is the salutation? | Yours faithfully | 12 Oak Road | *Dear Sam, | Monday 3 May
exercise: «The knight made a low salutation to the queen.» What does salutation suggest? | A kind of cake | Running away | A sword fight | *A bow or greeting that shows respect
test: «The knight made a low salutation to the queen.» What is a salutation? | *A bow or greeting that shows respect | A sword fight | A kind of cake | A type of horse
test: Which word is a jokey, old-fashioned hello? | Bye-bye | Goodbye | *Salutations! | Farewell
exam: Jules writes a letter to his gran. Which line is the salutation? | *Dear Gran, | Love from Jules | Thank you for the lovely present | 4 Park Lane
